[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3369708368","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109431#issuecomment-3369708368","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109431","id":3369708368,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7I2atQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-06T02:18:10Z","updated_at":"2025-10-06T02:18:10Z","body":"> As per my previous remarks, the only thing I'm not happy about is that we're pigeon holing ourselves into only supporting core composition layers.\r\n\r\nThis isn't any different from what we already have. The code for composition layers has had `switch` statements for the supported layer types since we first added support for composition layers in Godot 4.3.\r\n\r\nSo, this PR isn't really pigeon holing ourselves - we are already pigeon holed :-)\r\n\r\nWe can look at making composition layers more flexible, and able to support types that don't exist yet. But I don't see why that should hold up making what we already have safe for use with multi-threaded rendering? That could be addressed in a dedicated PR","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3369708368/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3369728784","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109431#issuecomment-3369728784","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109431","id":3369728784,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7I2fsQ","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-06T02:33:35Z","updated_at":"2025-10-06T02:33:35Z","body":"> We can look at making composition layers more flexible, and able to support types that don't exist yet.\r\n\r\nActually, now that I'm thinking about it, can already add support for composition layer types through GDExtension - they just wouldn't be exposed through the `OpenXRCompositionLayer` nodes.\r\n\r\nIn fact, we use `XR_TYPE_COMPOSITION_LAYER_PASSTHROUGH_FB` and `XR_TYPE_COMPOSITION_LAYER_PASSTHROUGH_HTC` from the godot_openxr_vendors repo\r\n\r\nThe `OpenXRCompositionLayerExtension` class modified here really only exists to support the `OpenXRCompositionLayer` nodes. So, the feature you're imagining would be adding new child classes to `OpenXRCompositionLayer` from GDExtension, I guess?\r\n\r\nAnyway, I still think that's unrelated to the goal of this PR, and that this PR doesn't make adding that feature any harder","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3369728784/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3415781852","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109431#issuecomment-3415781852","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109431","id":3415781852,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7LmLHc","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-17T14:11:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10